user: create a svelte app whit material ui components that sends a graphql query for getting anime titles and anime rating to anilist then display that info to the user in a clean way
---
assistant: To create a Svelte app with Material UI components that sends a GraphQL query for getting anime titles and ratings from AniList and displays that information to the user, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new Svelte app using the Svelte template in your preferred development environment.

2. Install the following dependencies:
``` 
npm install @material-ui/core @material-ui/icons apollo-boost graphql graphql-tag svelte-apollo
``` 
3. Create a new GraphQL client using Apollo Boost:
```
import ApolloClient from "apollo-boost";

const client = new ApolloClient({
  uri: "https://graphql.anilist.co",
});
```
4. Create a GraphQL query to fetch anime titles and ratings:
```
import gql from "graphql-tag";

const ANIME_QUERY = gql`
  query ($perPage: Int!, $page: Int!) {
    Page(perPage: $perPage, page: $page) {
      media(type: ANIME, sort: POPULARITY_DESC) {
        id
        title {
          romaji
          english
        }
        averageScore
      }
    }
  }
`;
```
5. Create a Svelte component to render the anime titles and ratings using Material UI components:
```
<script>
  import { query } from "svelte-apollo";
  import { ANIME_QUERY } from "./queries";

  const { loading, error, data } = query(ANIME_QUERY, {
    variables: {
      perPage: 10,
      page: 1,
    },
  });
</script>

{#if loading}
  <p>Loading...</p>
{:else if error}
  <p>Error: {error.message}</p>
{:else}
  <ul>
    {#each data.Page.media as anime}
      <li>
        <h2>{anime.title.english || anime.title.romaji}</h2>
        <p>Rating: {anime.averageScore}</p>
      </li>
    {/each}
  </ul>
{/if}
```
6. Style the component using Material UI:
```
<slot></slot>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Roboto", sans-serif;
  }
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  li {
    padding: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #333;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #666;
  }
</style>
```
7. Render the component in your main app component:
```
<template>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Anime Titles and Ratings</h1>
    <AnimeList />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
  import AnimeList from "./AnimeList.svelte";
</script>

<style>
  .container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 32px;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #333;
  }
</style>
```
That's it! You should now have a Svelte app that fetches anime titles and ratings from AniList using GraphQL and displays them using Material UI components.
